WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.003 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.272 line:92%
So, man, I am bad at breakups.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really am.
I don't even --

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you even ask
on these first dates now?

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What kind of music
do you like?"

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Who cares?

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is my new
first-date question --

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:18.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How likely are you
to yell at me in public?"

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.519 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
That one's going to
come in handy.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to be
in that relationship,

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.958
eight months in she's screaming
at me in front of strangers.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:28.228
I'm like, "It's cool.
We both like Chance The Rapper."

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in an Uber
right after the breakup.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you ever overshare
with the driver?

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.903 line:92%
Try to make a little connection.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.804 line:92%
He was like, "How are you?"

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"I just had a breakup."

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.108
He was like, "Let me tell you
some stuff about breakups."

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.643 line:92%
And the second he said that,

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.979 size:75% position:38%
I was like, "I think
I made a mistake."

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.981
He's like, "You know what I did
when my girlfriend left me?"

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:51.117
I said, "What?" He said,
"I had sex with everyone.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
You think that helped me?"
I was like, "No."

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.789 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He said, "It did."

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
All right.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like "You know
what else I did?

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
I called her up.
I told her all about it.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
You think that
made me feel better?"

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "God, no."
He said, "It did."

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"I'm going to stop guessing,

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause you're
very unpredictable."

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it went on like this
for 40 more minutes.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.103 line:92%
I finally got out of the car.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Do you think that
was helpful for me at all?"

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "Probably not."
I said, "It was."

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.109 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.611 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I Uber a lot.
I'm a terrible driver.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.486
You know, I'm a bad driver.
I get mad at other drivers, too.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.088 size:78% position:39%
You ever get cut off
by a reckless driver?

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.990
And then you catch up with them
to see what they look like?

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't matter
what race or gender.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every time I see
what they look like,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.297 line:92%
I'm always like, "I knew it."

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.632 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
Could just be a white guy.
I'm like, "Classic.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Classic white dude.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.875
Takes what's he wants,
contributes nothing to society."

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.411
I'm only going to do the example
for white people.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.847 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:57.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
But racism, that must be
learned behavior.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.451 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Don't you think?

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.285 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It must be.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Otherwise, you would meet
racist babies.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.058 line:92%
Which would be hilarious.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just itsy-bitsy
teeny-weeny racists.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.230 line:92%
"What were his first words?"

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.764 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"We'd rather not say.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:16.769 size:81% position:41%
Also, they were taken
out of context, so..."

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.405 line:92%
I've been drinking too much.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.373 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I really have.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:23.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
I peed on the street
the other night.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.812 line:92%
Yeah, I'm not bragging, but...

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.513 line:92%
This cop walked up to me.

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:29.616
He's like, "You are not
seriously peeing on the street?"

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:32.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "No, I'm doing it
ironically."

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.754
He handcuffed me while my penis
was still out,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:38.224
so that makes it look like
I committed a way worst crime

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.993 size:81% position:41% line:92%
than public urination.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of two times
I've been handcuffed drunk.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other time
I was in New Orleans.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was walking down the street.
19 years old.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.069 line:92%
And this guy on the street says,

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you want a hit
of this blunt?"

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:52.872 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I said, "Yes, I do."

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:53.673 line:92%
And the second I take a hit,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.808
these cops out of nowhere
slam me against the wall.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:56.476 size:88% position:44% line:92%
They're patting me down.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
This cop looks
deep into my eyes.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.779 line:92%
He goes, "You seem very drunk."

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
I look back,
and I go, "I am messed up."

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like,
"How much have you had?"

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"I've had a few too many."

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.489
He was like, "How much is that?"
I was like, "You know too many?"

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "Yeah." I was like,
"A few more than that."

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.026 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.227 line:92%
He didn't even crack a smile.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:17.230
I'm not saying I'm Oscar Wilde.
But I'm near blackout.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.631 line:92%
I deserve something, you know.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.700
So he's patting me down.
He feels in my back pocket.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.636
To this day, I have a little
notebook in my back pocket.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.771 line:92%
And he said, "What is that?"

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:27.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm drunk, so I said,
"That's my joke pad."

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's like,
"What the hell is a joke pad?"

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"I'm a stand-up comic."

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:37.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the second it came out
of my mouth, I was like, "No."

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.484 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.520
He's like, "You're a comedian?"
I said, "Yeah."

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.622 line:92%
He goes, "We'll see about that."

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
Takes the joke book
out of my back pocket,

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
starts reading the jokes
out loud.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
After every joke,
his partner would go,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Worst piece of crap
I've ever heard."

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
The two guys handcuffed
next to me

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.570 line:92%
are now laughing hysterically.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were supposed to be
on my side.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:00.573 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They flipped.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it only went on
two or three minutes.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.510
But it felt longer, 'cause
this guy's got no delivery.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's missing my key nuances.
You know?

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally uncuffs me.
He uncuffs the other guys.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.985 line:92%
They figured we had enough.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
They keep my joke book.
They drive away.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:15.622 line:92%
And the second they drive away,

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the guys I'm handcuffed
with turns to me.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.725 line:92%
He goes, "Oh, my God, dude.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.493 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I had cocaine on me.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.661 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:26.366
But they didn't search me
'cause of your horrible jokes."

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you so much.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.870 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.338 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You saved him.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey.
Thank you, brother.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:36.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Sam Morril.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
For tour dates,
go to sammorril.com.

